    "product_id": "3b274527-f831-408d-bd28-60a5ec8b88e4",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 140723\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1223 AM PDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts will continue through the \n  week with dry conditions and near-normal temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\n\nThe Desert Southwest will remain situated between an upper-level \ntrough across the Pacific Northwest and a ridge of high pressure \nacross the southern Plains. As a result, increased pressure \ngradients aloft will return gusty south-southwest winds to the \nregion each day through at least midweek. Expect gust speeds \ngenerally between 25 and 35 mph, though can't rule out 40 mph\nspeeds in isolated instances and/or in the higher terrain. \nOtherwise, expect mostly dry conditions and temperatures near-\nnormal. Near-normal for this time of year for desert valleys is \nin the upper-90s to lower-100s. Mid-to-late week, confidence \ndecreases. Ensemble means show a closed area of low pressure \npushing into the southwestern Great Basin Wednesday and Thursday, \nthen eventually meandering across the southern Great Basin heading\ninto the weekend. The associated upper-level jet overhead should \nprovide ample instability to our western zones. When combined with\nPWATs between 0.75 and 1.00 inches, portions of northwestern \nArizona could see a return of scattered showers and thunderstorms.\nWill continue to monitor as we get closer.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package...South-\nsouthwest winds continue through the TAF period, strongest from late \nmorning through sunset with gusts 15-25 knots. Clear skies with \ntemperatures near 100F from 21z to 00z.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Light breezes tonight \ngive way to southerly to westerly winds again Monday afternoon. \nStrongest breezes broadly along and southeast of the I-15 corridor \nwhere gusts of 15-15 knots are likely (80%). Mostly clear skies with \njust a few mid-level clouds in northwestern AZ and the Colorado \nRiver Valley. Isolated showers/storms possible (30%) in far \neastern/northeastern Mohave County in the afternoon hours.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Soulat\nAVIATION...Woods\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
